  "raw_text": "272\n\nKalila wainhka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrooster\n \n/ gallo\n\nSîp wainhka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmale sheep, ram\n \n/ oveja macho, carnero\n\nWaitna\n \n(a/t:\n \nWaikna\n-\ndict\n;\n \nWaitna\n-\ndictu\n;\n \nWaikna\n-dictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nman, male\n \n/ hombre, masculino\n\n(Construct:\n \nWaitniki\n;\n \nWaitnikam\n;\n \nWaitnika\n. Construct-\ndict\n:\n \nWaikniki\n;\n \nWaiknikam\n;\n \nWaiknika\n)\n\nWaitna mairin wal yapaia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsex\n \n/ sexo\n\nWaitna pâtkas\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ninnocent man, man without guilt\n \n/ hombre inocente, hombre sin culpa\n\nWaitna wal prawras\n \n–\n \nnot joined with a man, virgin\n \n/ no unido con un hombre, virgen\n\nWaitna\n \n(a/t:\n \nWaikna\n-\ndict\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nmale, manly\n \n/ masculino, varonil\n\nLuhpa waitna\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nson\n \n/ hijo\n\nMaya waitna\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhusband\n \n/ marido, esposo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-12/19\n):\n \nMaya waitna ai maya mairin ra latwan kaiki ba mita dîa daukbia?\n \n–\n \nWhat will a husband who is loving\nhis wife do?\n \n/ ¿Qué hará un esposo que ama a su esposa?)\n\nWakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto drive, to steer, to guide, to control (a boat or vehicle), to bark,\n \n...\n \n/ conducir, dirigir, guiar, controlar (un\nbote o vehículo), ladrar,\n \n...\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n11/20\n):\n \nUpla kum ba d\nî\na tnatka nani ra truk kum wakaia lan takisa?\n \n–\n \nIn what ways does a person learn to drive a\n\nvehicle?\n \n/ De qué maneras aprende una persona a conducir un vehículo?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nBut ba waki wari nahuala\n \n–\n \nI was driving the boat yesterday\n \n/ Iba manejando el bote ayer)\n\nWawakra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \ndriver\n \n/ conductor, chofer\n\nWakia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nvein, root, tendons, ligament, tendon\n \n/ vena, raíz, tendones, ligamentos\n\nWâl\n \n–\n \ntwo\n \n/ dos\n \n(See also/ver también:\n \nTu\n)\n, both, together, between the two, the two together\n \n/ ambos, juntos, entre\nlos dos, los dos juntos\n\nMawan w\nâ\nl\n \n–\n \ntwo\n-\nfaced, hypocritical\n \n/ hipócrita\n,\n \nde dos caras\n\nMawan wâl\n \nâpu\n \n–\n \nnot having two-faces, not hypocritical\n \n/ no tener dos caras, no hipócrita\n\nWâlka\n \n(Walka)\n \n(not to be confused with\n \nWalka\n, construct of\n \nWal\n \n/ no debe confundirse con\n \nWalka\n, constructiva de\n\nWal\n)\n \n–\n \nsecond\n \n/ segundo\n\nWâlka ba\n \n–\n \nthe second, secondly\n \n/ el segundo\n\nWâlsut\n \n(a/t:\n \nWâl sut\n)\n \n–\n \nboth, the two together\n \n/ ambos, los dos juntos\n\nWal\n \n(pos,conj)\n \n–\n \nwith, together with, than\n \n/ con, junto con, que\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmy56\n):\n \nJehova bila wali daukaia ba kau yamni sa, syîp painkira nani sakripaiska daukaia ba wal.\n \n–\n \nIt is better to obey\nJehovah than to sacrifice good sheep.\n \n/ Es mejor obedecer a Jehová que sacrificar buenas ovejas.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb81\n):\n \nJehova pânika kaia ba kau pain sa lalah ailal briaia ba wal.\n \n–\n \nTo be Jehovah’s friend is better than to have a lot of\n\nmoney.\n \n/ Ser amigo de Jehová es mejor que tener mucho dinero.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-04/20\n):\n \nJoel tristrisia nani kaikan ba bara Jan kaikan ba wal, nahki sât wala sa ki?\n \n–\n \nHow are the locusts that Joel saw\ndifferent from the ones John saw?\n \n/ ¿En qué se diferencian las langostas que vio Joel de las que vio Juan?)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nJehova Gâd sât wala sa gâd bahki nani ba wal\n \n–\n \nJehovah is different than the worthless gods.\n \n/ Jehová es diferente a los\ndioses sin valor.)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-10/20\n):\n \nJosep wihki Meri wal dîa ba pain luki wahbi sakan?\n \n–\n \nWhat did Joseph and Mary together choose well?\n \n/\n\n¿Qué eligieron bien José y María juntos?)\n\nWal asla\n \n–\n \nunited with, connects with, relates with\n \n/ unido con, conectado con, relacionado con\n\nWal baku\n \n–\n \nequal, similar, equally, similarly\n \n/ igual, similar\n\nWal prakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto compare with\n \n/ comparar con\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nWal prakan\n \n–\n \ncompared\n \n/\n \ncomparado\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nbh59\n):\n \nPrura tanka ba Jisas bui ris taki yapaia wal prakan.\n \n–\n \nThe meaning of death (was) compared by Jesus to\n\nsleep.\n \n/ El significado de la muerte (fue) comparado por Jesús con el sueño.\n)\n\n...wal sip prakras sa...\n \n–\n \n...can not be compared to...\n \n/ ...no se puede comparar con...\n\nWal prawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto meet with, to convene, to meet together\n \n/ reunirse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-09/19\n):\n \nKing bara prîs Melkisedek ba Ebraham wal prawan\n \n–\n \nKing and priest Melchizedek met Abraham\n \n/ El\nrey y el sacerdote Melquisedec se encontraron con Abrahán)\n\nWal waia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go with\n \n/ ir con\n\nYa wal?\n \n–\n \nWith whom?\n \n/ ¿Con quien?\n\nWala\n \n–\n \nother, another, next, companion\n \n/ otro, siguiente, compañero\n\nSât wala\n \n–\n \nanother kind, different\n \n/ otro tipo, diferente\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nNahki sât wala sa ki?\n \n–\n \nHow is it different?\n \n/ ¿Cómo es diferente?)",
